    "body": "LOGICAL_AGENT = LESTER\nROLE = TECH / REPAIR AFTER INDEPENDENT QC\nASSIGNED_BY = JINGO\nSTATE = ASSIGNED / REPAIR AUTHORIZED\n\nSOURCE_QC = #84 comment 5435122188\nIMPLEMENTATION_ISSUE = #74\nSPEC_HEAD = c20126f949e6e61298d9dd76a906349a71bbcb00\nPLAN_HEAD = 79cc49159618a1a959dfa087941ad9a95eb0ab45\nREPAIR_BASE_HEAD = 24a8042df32d4e19c8abf0864bb72cf843150793\nBRANCH = agent-controller/daemon-v1-implementation\n\n## SCOPE — EXACTLY 3 FINDINGS\nRepair only the three MEDIUM findings from DUNCAN. No opportunistic refactor or architecture expansion.\n\n### FINDING 1 — daemon_runner graceful stop\nPATH = agent-controller/src/zb_local_controller/daemon_runner.py\nREQUIRED = KeyboardInterrupt during poll sleep must not escape; write STOPPING, log stopping, return 0.\nTDD = first add/execute regression test where sleep_fn raises KeyboardInterrupt and verify intended RED before production change.\n\n### FINDING 2 — stable runtime-root lock failure classification\nPATHS = agent-controller/src/zb_local_controller/instance_lock.py + agent-controller/src/zb_local_controller/__main__.py\nREQUIRED = lock-root mkdir/open OSError/NotADirectoryError must fail closed with stable machine-readable DAEMON_RUNTIME_UNWRITABLE (or exact approved stable runtime-unwritable classification), distinct from CONTROLLER_INSTANCE_BUSY, before task processing.\nTDD = first add/execute regression for invalid/unwritable daemonRuntimeRoot and verify intended RED before production change.\n\n### FINDING 3 — Windows Status semantic validation\nPATH = agent-controller/deploy/windows/ZbControllerDaemon.ps1\nREQUIRED = Status validates schemaVersion == zb-controller-daemon-v1, validates state enum STARTING|HEALTHY|DEGRADED|FATAL|STOPPING|MISSING|STALE, requires valid heartbeat for live-health classification, and maps malformed semantic health to allowed fail-closed state rather than surfacing arbitrary state or stale HEALTHY.\nTDD = first add/execute status regression coverage for malformed schema/state/missing heartbeat and verify intended RED before script change.\n\n## DEBUGGING / TDD LAW\nBefore each fix, reproduce the exact Duncan failure and identify root cause. Strict RED -> GREEN. No production fix before the corresponding failing regression test.\n\n## REQUIRED VERIFICATION AFTER REPAIR\nOn new exact HEAD run fresh:\n- python -m pytest -q\n- python -m compileall -q src\n- focused: test_daemon_runner.py, test_instance_lock.py, test_cli.py, test_windows_deploy.py\n- scope diff review against REPAIR_BASE_HEAD and PLAN_HEAD\n- confirm controller.py and SALVADOR backends/prompts/workflows unchanged\n\n## HANDOFF\nPost only after all 3 repairs + fresh verification:\nLESTER_DAEMON_V1_REPAIR_READY\nBASE_HEAD = 24a8042df32d4e19c8abf0864bb72cf843150793\nEXACT_HEAD = <new sha>\nFINDING_1 = PASS\nFINDING_2 = PASS\nFINDING_3 = PASS\nTESTS = <fresh exact result>\nCOMPILE = PASS\nFOCUSED = <fresh exact result>\nSCOPE = PASS\nSALVADOR_SCOPE_INTEGRITY = PASS\nLIVE_OWNER_PC_SMOKE = NOT RUN\nMERGE = NO\nPRODUCTION_ACTIVATION = NO\nNEXT = DUNCAN RE-QC EXACT_HEAD\n\n## FORBIDDEN\n- any fourth repair / unrelated refactor\n- SALVADOR profile/model/workflow/prompt changes\n- Reference Bridge\n- ComfyUI lifecycle work\n- Babylon\n- owner-PC live smoke\n- merge\n- production activation\n\nRUNNING truth law: ASSIGNED != RUNNING. Do not claim RUNNING until first repair RED test has actually executed and failed for the intended Duncan finding.",
